<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka tea shares rise on growth prospects.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka tea shares rise on growth prospects.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of firms in Sri Lanka's plantation sector, rose in early Thursday trade, mainly due to tea prices which are expected to be buoyant in 1997, brokers said.</p>
<p>Tea Smallholder Factories was 7.69 percent or four rupees up at 56, Kelani Valley Plantations 5.3 percent or 1.75 rupees up at 34.75, Horana Plantations 4.48 percent or 1.50 rupees up at 35.</p>
<p>&quot;Retailers are buying the shares because they are seen doing well due to continuing demand from the Commonwealth of Independent states and the Middle East,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
